 "notes": "Solid dark-red 'Yb+ E3/E2' curve of Fig. 2 (file fainv_ver4.pdf in the e-print), the paper's measured 95% CL bound on the QCD axion gluon coupling 1/f_a from 235 days of the PTB single-ion 171Yb+ E3/E2 frequency-ratio comparison. Curve extracted from the vector PDF (stroke color 0.698,0.133,0.133, solid; the same-color dashed path is the 1e-18-amplitude projection and was excluded), axes calibrated from tick marks (x: 1e-23..1e-17 eV, y: 1e-19..1e-11 GeV^-1, both log). Noisy polyline reduced to per-log-bin medians (~15 bins/decade). Calibration cross-checked with Eq. (13): amplitude limit 2e-17, K_E3,E2=2.4e-3, beta=-0.34 reproduce 1/f_a~2e-12 GeV^-1 at the maximum mass, matching the curve; max mass 1.03e-17 eV = pi*0.005Hz*hbar (signal oscillates at 2 m_a), consistent with the stated 0.005 Hz analysis cutoff. Curve clipped to the plotted mass range (>=1e-23 eV); paper notes the all-DM assumption should be relaxed below ~1e-22 eV but plots the constraint without that correction. The paper also bounds scalar couplings d_g and d_mhat (Fig. 1/3); the axion 1/f_a bound is reported here as the compilation-relevant result.",
